WEBVTT

00:07.862 --> 00:09.172
- Are you ready, kids?
- 孩子们，你们准备好了吗？

00:09.206 --> 00:10.862
all:
Aye, aye, Captain!
全部：
是啊是啊，队长！

00:10.896 --> 00:12.344
- I can't hear you.
- 我听不到你说话。

00:12.379 --> 00:14.482
all:
Aye, aye, Captain!
全部：
是啊是啊，队长！

00:14.517 --> 00:17.344
- ♪ Ohh...
- ♪ 哦...

00:17.379 --> 00:19.413
♪ Who lives in a pineapple
under the sea? ♪
♪ 谁住在菠萝里
在海底？ ♪

00:19.448 --> 00:21.413
all:
SpongeBob SquarePants!
全部：
海绵宝宝！

00:21.448 --> 00:23.344
- ♪ Absorbent and yellow
and porous is he ♪
- ♪ 吸水性和黄色
他是多孔的 ♪

00:23.379 --> 00:25.206
all:
SpongeBob SquarePants!
全部：
海绵宝宝！

00:25.241 --> 00:27.448
- ♪ If nautical nonsense
be something you wish ♪
- ♪ 如果航海废话
成为你想要的东西♪

00:27.482 --> 00:29.344
all:
SpongeBob SquarePants!
全部：
海绵宝宝！

00:29.379 --> 00:31.413
- ♪ Then drop on the deck
and flop like a fish ♪
- ♪ 然后落在甲板上
然后像鱼一样扑通扑通♪

00:31.448 --> 00:33.413
all: SpongeBob SquarePants!
- Ready?
所有：海绵宝宝！
- 准备好？

00:33.448 --> 00:35.310
all:
SpongeBob SquarePants!
全部：
海绵宝宝！

00:35.344 --> 00:37.620
SpongeBob SquarePants!
海绵宝宝！

00:37.655 --> 00:39.551
SpongeBob
SquarePants!
海绵宝宝
方裤！

00:39.586 --> 00:40.896
- SpongeBob
- 海绵宝宝

00:40.931 --> 00:42.758
SquarePants!
方裤！

00:42.793 --> 00:45.482
[laughing]
[笑]

00:45.517 --> 00:47.758
♪
♪
♪
♪

00:47.793 --> 00:49.413
[waves crashing]
[海浪拍打]

00:51.413 --> 00:54.379
[playful music]
[俏皮的音乐]

00:54.413 --> 01:00.586
♪
♪
♪
♪

01:00.620 --> 01:02.206
[bubbling]
[thump]
[冒泡]
[扑通]

01:02.241 --> 01:05.586
[tense music]
[overlapping chatter]
[紧张的音乐]
[重叠的喋喋不休]

01:05.620 --> 01:08.413
- Mr. Squidward.
- 章鱼哥先生。

01:08.448 --> 01:10.931
What is happening
in me restaurant?
正在发生什么
在我的餐厅？

01:10.965 --> 01:12.724
- The customers
have gone crazy.
- 客户
已经疯了。

01:12.758 --> 01:14.034
- Ah!
- 啊！

01:14.068 --> 01:16.689
- SpongeBob is late for work,
so there's no food.
- 海绵宝宝上班迟到了
所以没有食物。

01:16.724 --> 01:20.379
- [gasps] But he's never been
late for work in his life.
- [喘气] 但他从来没有
他一生中上班迟到。

01:20.413 --> 01:24.689
Oh, this can only mean
one thing.
哦，这只能说明
一件事。

01:24.724 --> 01:25.965
[bell rings]
[铃声响起]

01:26.000 --> 01:28.448
SpongeBob has passed away.
海绵宝宝去世了。

01:28.482 --> 01:29.793
all: [gasps]
全体：[喘气]

01:29.827 --> 01:31.551
[sobbing]
[抽泣]

01:31.586 --> 01:34.551
[solemn music]
[庄严的音乐]

01:34.586 --> 01:36.275
♪
♪
♪
♪

01:36.310 --> 01:39.724
- Or... maybe he's just
seriously injured.
- 或者...也许他只是
重伤。

01:39.758 --> 01:41.206
[chuckles]
[笑声]

01:41.241 --> 01:42.655
all: [sobbing]
- Oh, yeah,
全体：[抽泣]
- 哦，是的，

01:42.689 --> 01:44.310
that's still bad, isn't it?
那还是很糟糕，不是吗？

01:44.344 --> 01:46.620
[sobs]
[抽泣]

01:46.655 --> 01:50.758
- I had no idea you cared
that much about SpongeBob.
- 我不知道你在乎
关于海绵宝宝就这么多了。

01:50.793 --> 01:52.551
- Of course.
- 当然。

01:52.586 --> 01:55.034
He's been a loyal employee.
他一直是一名忠诚的员工。

01:55.068 --> 02:00.103
His passing would be a great
loss to me bank account.
他的去世将是一个伟大的
我的银行账户遭受损失。

02:00.137 --> 02:02.689
Oh, I--to me personally,
of course.
哦，我——就我个人而言，
当然。

02:02.724 --> 02:04.103
Now, come on,
现在，来吧，

02:04.137 --> 02:07.172
we have to go check on
SpongeBob's possible remains.
我们得去检查一下
海绵宝宝可能仍然存在。

02:07.206 --> 02:09.344
- With pleasure.
- 荣幸。

02:09.379 --> 02:12.103
- [groans]
- What? Too soon?
- [呻吟]
- 什么？太快了？

02:12.137 --> 02:14.068
[bubbling]
[冒泡]

02:14.103 --> 02:15.482
[solemn music]
[庄严的音乐]

02:15.517 --> 02:19.862
- Prepare yourselves
for the horror.
- 做好准备
为了恐怖。

02:19.896 --> 02:21.137
Or the joy.
或者说是喜悦。

02:21.172 --> 02:22.793
Let's not be downers
about this.
我们不要成为沮丧的人
关于这个。

02:22.827 --> 02:24.172
- Oh, yeah.
- Okay.
- 哦，是的。
- 好的。

02:24.206 --> 02:25.965
- But probably, like I said,
- 但也许，就像我说的，

02:26.000 --> 02:28.517
the horror.
恐怖。

02:28.551 --> 02:30.482
all: [gasp]
全体：[喘气]

02:30.517 --> 02:32.724
[door creaks open]
[门嘎吱一声打开]

02:32.758 --> 02:35.620
[whispering chatter]
[窃窃私语]

02:35.655 --> 02:37.724
[suspenseful music]
[悬疑音乐]

02:37.758 --> 02:39.827
- Neptune's nightmare.
- 海王星的噩梦。

02:39.862 --> 02:42.586
That snail is eating
SpongeBob's face.
那只蜗牛正在吃东西
海绵宝宝的脸。

02:42.620 --> 02:44.413
Get away from him.
离他远点。

02:44.448 --> 02:46.068
- [groans]
- [呻吟]

02:46.103 --> 02:47.931
[overlapping chatter]
- Such a nice kid.
[重叠的喋喋不休]
- 真是个好孩子。

02:47.965 --> 02:49.896
- I--I...
[babbles]
- 我--我...
[胡言乱语]

02:49.931 --> 02:51.862
Oh, good morning, everyone.
哦，大家早上好。

02:51.896 --> 02:53.517
[upbeat music]
[欢快的音乐]

02:53.551 --> 02:56.758
[disappointed chatter]
[失望的喋喋不休]

02:56.793 --> 02:59.206
- SpongeBob, you're alive!
- 海绵宝宝，你还活着！

02:59.241 --> 03:01.172
- I am?
Well, thank goodness.
- 我是？
好吧，谢天谢地。

03:01.206 --> 03:02.482
Wait, why wouldn't I be alive?
等等，我为什么不能活着？

03:02.517 --> 03:05.655
- You were late to work,
so we assumed the worst.
- 你上班迟到了，
所以我们做了最坏的打算。

03:05.689 --> 03:07.137
- You mean "the best."
- 你的意思是“最好的”。

03:07.172 --> 03:10.413
- Late to work?
But that's impossible.
- 上班迟到？
但这是不可能的。

03:10.448 --> 03:13.000
My trusty alarm clock
always waked me up.
我值得信赖的闹钟
总是叫醒我。

03:13.034 --> 03:14.551
See?
Ah.
看？
啊。

03:14.586 --> 03:17.482
Well, how do you like that?
It's unplugged.
嗯，你觉得怎么样？
它已拔掉插头。

03:17.517 --> 03:19.965
Well, we'll just fix that
and I'll never be late again.
好吧，我们会解决这个问题
我再也不会迟到了。

03:20.000 --> 03:21.896
Oh.
[grunts]
哦。
[咕哝]

03:21.931 --> 03:23.862
[playful music]
[俏皮的音乐]

03:23.896 --> 03:26.275
- [grunts]
- [咕哝]

03:26.310 --> 03:27.862
Ah.
啊。

03:27.896 --> 03:30.310
- Oh, my clock!
- 哦，我的时钟！

03:30.344 --> 03:33.551
- Huh? Ah.
- Mm?
- 啊？啊。
- 毫米？

03:33.586 --> 03:35.931
Looks like you need
a new clock, boyo.
看起来你需要
一个新时钟，博约。

03:35.965 --> 03:39.103
- Oh, I could never replace
my old clock, Mr. Krabs.
- 哦，我永远无法取代
我的老钟，蟹老板。

03:39.137 --> 03:40.965
We've been through
too much together.
我们已经经历过
在一起太多了。

03:41.000 --> 03:43.206
It's the only alarm clock
I've ever owned.
这是唯一的闹钟
我曾经拥有过。

03:43.241 --> 03:44.965
I can fix it.
我可以修好它。

03:45.000 --> 03:46.137
- Eh, good luck.
- 呃，祝你好运。

03:46.172 --> 03:48.482
But you better
not be late tomorrow.
但你最好
明天不迟到。

03:48.517 --> 03:51.862
Or else.
否则。

03:51.896 --> 03:55.724
- Did that stupid clock
give me a bump on my head?
- 那个愚蠢的时钟吗？
给我撞一下我的头吗？

03:55.758 --> 03:58.620
- [scream]
both: Ugh.
- [尖叫]
两人：呃。

03:58.655 --> 04:01.137
- [snoring]
- Oh, come on, come on.
- [打鼾]
-哦，来吧，来吧。

04:01.172 --> 04:04.000
I still love you.
Let me fix you.
我依然爱你。
让我来修复你。

04:04.034 --> 04:05.206
Wow!
哇！

04:05.241 --> 04:07.448
- [grunts, gulps, exhales]
- [咕哝，吞咽，呼气]

04:07.482 --> 04:11.379
Ooh, hey, SpongeBob,
what're you doing?
哦，嘿，海绵宝宝，
你在做什么？

04:11.413 --> 04:12.586
- Mm.
- 毫米。

04:12.620 --> 04:14.724
Oh, I'm just trying to fix
this old alarm clock.
哦，我只是想修复
这个旧闹钟。

04:14.758 --> 04:17.034
I'm gonna need that part you
swallowed, by the way.
我需要你的那部分
顺便说一下，被吞掉了。

04:17.068 --> 04:18.413
- That's cool.
- 这很酷。

04:18.448 --> 04:20.275
Just give me a couple of hours.
给我几个小时。

04:20.310 --> 04:24.862
You know, I could totally fix
your clock for you.
你知道，我完全可以解决
你的时钟。

04:24.896 --> 04:26.172
[laughs]
[笑]

04:26.206 --> 04:27.448
- Oh, I don't know, Patrick.
- 哦，我不知道，帕特里克。

04:27.482 --> 04:29.241
This clock means a lot to me
and...
这个时钟对我来说意义重大
还有……

04:29.275 --> 04:30.379
- [eager giggle]
- [急切的咯咯笑]

04:30.413 --> 04:31.896
- Well, okay, are you sure?
- 好吧，你确定吗？

04:31.931 --> 04:35.517
- Absolutely.
Don't you worry.
- 绝对地。
别担心。

04:35.551 --> 04:39.758
I promise to be super careful.
我保证会超级小心。

04:39.793 --> 04:43.448
[grunting, groaning]
[咕哝，呻吟]

04:43.482 --> 04:45.137
- Ah!
- 啊！

04:45.172 --> 04:48.482
- Why don't you fix?
- 你为什么不修好？

04:48.517 --> 04:51.965
[screaming]
[尖叫]

04:52.000 --> 04:54.586
[tense music]
[紧张的音乐]

04:54.620 --> 04:56.448
Hmm?
Uh...
唔？
呃...

04:56.482 --> 04:58.551
Sorry, SpongeBob,
I couldn't fix it.
对不起，海绵宝宝，
我无法修复它。

04:58.586 --> 05:00.068
- Thanks for trying, Patrick,
- 谢谢你的尝试，帕特里克，

05:00.103 --> 05:01.827
but I guess nothing
lasts forever.
但我猜没什么
永远持续下去。

05:01.862 --> 05:04.034
Looks like I'm gonna need
a new clock after all.
看来我需要
毕竟是一个新时钟。

05:04.068 --> 05:05.931
- Hmm!
[laughs]
- 唔！
[笑]

05:05.965 --> 05:08.068
In that case...
在这种情况下...

05:08.103 --> 05:10.068
[grunts]
[咕哝]

05:10.103 --> 05:11.862
[bubbling]
[冒泡]

05:11.896 --> 05:14.862
[lively music]
[活泼的音乐]

05:14.896 --> 05:17.000
- Um, hello?
- 嗯，你好？

05:17.034 --> 05:18.448
- Hello, there.
- 你好呀。

05:18.482 --> 05:21.724
Welcome to Clock World,
where we always have time
欢迎来到时钟世界，
我们总是有时间的地方

05:21.758 --> 05:23.034
for a bargain.
为了讨价还价。

05:23.068 --> 05:24.931
How can I help you?
我怎么帮你？

05:24.965 --> 05:27.620
- Do you have another alarm
clock like my old one?
- 你还有另一个闹钟吗
时钟像我的旧时钟一样吗？

05:27.655 --> 05:29.034
[plops]
[扑通扑通]

05:29.068 --> 05:31.931
- Hmm?
- 唔？

05:31.965 --> 05:34.413
[tongue slurps,
palatal click]
[舌头发出声音，
腭音]

05:34.448 --> 05:37.896
Ah, the 740 Foghorn
Wake-Em-Up Grand.
啊，740 雾号
唤醒他们盛大。

05:37.931 --> 05:41.000
I'm sorry to say they don't
make this model anymore.
很遗憾他们没有
不再做这个模型了。

05:41.034 --> 05:43.482
But if you have a second,
但如果你还有时间的话

05:43.517 --> 05:46.206
I have many others
I can show you. [giggles]
我还有很多其他的
我可以给你看。 [咯咯笑]

05:46.241 --> 05:48.758
- Wow. So many to choose from.
- 哇。有这么多可供选择。

05:48.793 --> 05:50.896
Oh, I'll never be able
to choose a clock
哦，我永远无法
选择时钟

05:50.931 --> 05:52.137
with this many choices.
有这么多选择。

05:52.172 --> 05:53.965
- I'll just take 'em all.
- 我会把它们全部拿走。

05:54.000 --> 05:55.862
- Ah!, I'm rich.
- 啊！，我很有钱。

05:55.896 --> 05:58.862
[maniacal laughter]
Whoo!
[疯狂的笑声]
呼！

05:58.896 --> 06:00.689
Whoo, whoo, whoo, whoo!
呼、呼、呼、呼！

06:00.724 --> 06:03.000
[upbeat music]
[欢快的音乐]

06:03.034 --> 06:06.862
♪
♪
♪
♪

06:08.862 --> 06:09.931
- [meows]
- [喵]

06:09.965 --> 06:12.827
- My old foghorn clock was
the only alarm clock
- 我的旧雾号钟是
唯一的闹钟

06:12.862 --> 06:14.034
that could wake me up.
这可以叫醒我。

06:14.068 --> 06:15.827
Sure hope one of these works.
当然希望这些作品之一。

06:15.862 --> 06:18.241
Goodnight, Gare-bear.
晚安，车站熊。

06:18.275 --> 06:20.103
[gargle snoring]
[漱口打鼾]

06:20.137 --> 06:21.655
[tranquil music]
[安静的音乐]

06:21.689 --> 06:23.241
[bell rings]
[铃声响起]

06:23.275 --> 06:25.965
[gargles]
[漱口]

06:26.000 --> 06:27.793
[snores]
[打鼾]

06:27.827 --> 06:29.931
male narrator:
One hour later...
男旁白：
一小时后...

06:29.965 --> 06:31.172
[rooster crows]
- Huh?
[公鸡打鸣]
- 啊？

06:31.206 --> 06:32.896
[babbling]
[胡说]

06:32.931 --> 06:36.137
[grunts]
[咕哝]

06:36.172 --> 06:37.896
- Late.
- 晚的。

06:37.931 --> 06:40.034
- I hope this one works.
- 我希望这个能起作用。

06:40.068 --> 06:41.758
[squeals]
[尖叫声]

06:41.793 --> 06:43.620
[snoring]
[打鼾]

06:43.655 --> 06:45.068
[dramatic music]
[bell rings]
[戏剧音乐]
[铃声响起]

06:45.103 --> 06:46.482
- [groans]
- [呻吟]

06:46.517 --> 06:48.172
narrator: Late again...
旁白：又迟到了……

06:48.206 --> 06:51.275
- [panting]
- [气喘吁吁]

06:51.310 --> 06:52.620
- Late.
- 晚的。

06:52.655 --> 06:54.034
- [snoring]
- [打鼾]

06:54.068 --> 06:57.482
♪
♪
♪
♪

06:57.517 --> 06:58.413
Huh?
啊？

06:58.448 --> 06:59.551
[jellyfish buzz]
[水母嗡嗡声]

06:59.586 --> 07:01.862
narrator: You get the idea.
旁白：你明白了。

07:01.896 --> 07:03.793
- Late.
- 晚的。

07:03.827 --> 07:05.000
Late.
晚的。

07:05.034 --> 07:06.103
Late.
晚的。

07:06.137 --> 07:08.275
Still late.
Late.
还是迟到了。
晚的。

07:08.310 --> 07:11.413
Late, late, late, late, late,
late, late.
迟到，迟到，迟到，迟到，迟到，
迟到了，迟到了。

07:11.448 --> 07:13.482
- Still late.
- [whimpers]
- 还是迟到了。
- [呜咽]

07:13.517 --> 07:16.551
- Late again.
- 又迟到了。

07:16.586 --> 07:19.620
I told you before
that you best not be late
我之前告诉过你
你最好不要迟到

07:19.655 --> 07:20.793
or else.
或者其他。

07:20.827 --> 07:24.206
But this time,
I'll be emphasizing it
但这一次，
我会强调一下

07:24.241 --> 07:26.724
with a furrowed brow.
皱着眉头。

07:26.758 --> 07:30.034
Or else.
否则。

07:30.068 --> 07:31.551
[bubbling]
[冒泡]

07:31.586 --> 07:35.482
- Oh, I don't know how many
more "or elses" I can take.
- 哦，我不知道有多少
我可以接受更多的“否则”。

07:35.517 --> 07:37.862
I have to figure out a way
to wake up on time.
我得想个办法
准时起床。

07:37.896 --> 07:39.172
[alarm rings]
[警报响起]

07:39.206 --> 07:41.586
- [meows excitedly]
- [兴奋地喵喵叫]

07:41.620 --> 07:43.724
[lively music]
[bell rings]
[活泼的音乐]
[铃声响起]

07:43.758 --> 07:46.413
♪
♪
♪
♪

07:46.448 --> 07:49.068
- Hey, what a great idea.
- 嘿，真是个好主意。

07:49.103 --> 07:52.241
[panting]
[气喘吁吁]

07:52.275 --> 07:59.482
♪
♪
♪
♪

08:01.965 --> 08:05.034
Oh.
[moans]
哦。
[呻吟声]

08:05.068 --> 08:07.103
[snoring]
[打鼾]

08:07.137 --> 08:11.448
[alarm blaring]
[警报声]

08:11.482 --> 08:14.586
[bell rings]
[铃声响起]

08:14.620 --> 08:17.793
[playful music]
[俏皮的音乐]

08:17.827 --> 08:19.000
[thump]
[扑通]

08:19.034 --> 08:20.413
